# COLD frontend environment variables.
#
# VITE_-prefixed variables are inlined into the browser bundle by Vite, so
# nothing secret may ever go here — see supabase/functions/live-data/README.md
# for where real provider keys belong (server-side Edge Function env vars only).

# Public URL of the COLD LIVE data backend (a Supabase Edge Function). This is
# not a secret — it is just the address of our own API boundary. Leave empty
# (the default) to use local fixture data only, with zero network calls.
VITE_LIVE_DATA_URL=

# Server-side only (Supabase Edge Function environment, NOT this file's
# VITE_ variables). Comma-separated list of origins the live-data function
# will attach access-control-allow-origin for. Documented here as a name
# placeholder only; the actual value is configured in the Supabase project,
# never committed.
# LIVE_DATA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Server-side only. Required by SEC's fair-access policy: every request to
# data.sec.gov must carry a descriptive User-Agent identifying the app and a
# real contact address. Expected form (placeholder — do not commit a real
# contact address):
# SEC_EDGAR_USER_AGENT=COLD Ownership Simulator contact@example.com
